  "scope": "The literal160-slot machine traverses the actual original stored rational row, retains each original head across the real recursive tail call, adds the same original scalar through the unchanged actual canonical rational table, and prepends each returned record. It produces the exact original BinaryFractionalGuesses.shifted raw row, in the original order including duplicates, with both input representations retained. A same-run terminal-inclusive physical bound depends only on original row length and padded numerator/denominator bit lengths. Both original table representation directions are proved. The scalar value, original input heap representations, initial H/A and dense cursor remain inputs; computed-lambda handover and complete guess/solver composition remain separate. Twelve physical cases independently specify raw output rows, including unreduced zero/duplicate/padded values.",
